      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You bring up a valid point about anachronism; judging ancient figures by modern moral standards overlooks the brutal realities of Athenian power politics. In a system where ambitious men often faced ultimate punishment for perceived disloyalty, maneuvering might indeed have been a calculated risk to avoid a worse fate. Therefore, one could argue his actions were a desperate, albeit destructive, attempts to gain security within a ruthless political structure.",
